WEBVTT

00:00:00.020 --> 00:00:03.230
<b>Sohoku High School
Bicycle Racing Club</b>

00:00:03.230 --> 00:00:07.190
<b>Sohoku High School
 Bicycle Racing Club</b>

00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:13.820
Diving into a futon after a bath is the best.

00:00:15.230 --> 00:00:17.860
Nothing beats a post-race soak
in the hot springs!

00:00:17.860 --> 00:00:20.370
The Inter-High sure picks
great venues every year!

00:00:20.370 --> 00:00:24.080
Some of my lower-body muscles are still sore.

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:28.000
The race today was really tough.

00:00:29.910 --> 00:00:30.710
Yeah.

00:00:30.710 --> 00:00:34.470
Oh, sorry! Did that bring back bad thoughts?

00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:36.490
Today's finish line...

00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:39.370
It's fine.

00:00:39.370 --> 00:00:40.890
What's done is done.

00:00:41.370 --> 00:00:44.390
I'm sorry for letting you down.

00:00:44.390 --> 00:00:45.780
That's not...

00:00:45.780 --> 00:00:48.020
I disappointed myself.

00:00:49.220 --> 00:00:53.150
When you're disappointed, you must
let go and feel as disappointed as you can.

00:00:54.140 --> 00:00:56.470
Feel disappointed, get pissed off,

00:00:56.470 --> 00:00:59.800
think of everything you would 
have done differently,

00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:02.710
regret it all, cry,

00:01:03.130 --> 00:01:04.330
and sleep.

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:05.430
<i>Naruko-kun...</i>

00:01:06.550 --> 00:01:10.090
And then, forget it all
the next day and snap back.

00:01:11.090 --> 00:01:13.880
That's Naruko's flashy snap back technique!

00:01:17.090 --> 00:01:17.910
Yeah!

00:01:24.850 --> 00:01:26.640
<b><i>Yowamushi Pedal</i></b>

00:01:26.810 --> 00:01:28.730
<b><i>Yowamushi Pedal</i></b>

00:02:49.490 --> 00:02:52.260
Okay, time to eat!

00:02:50.830 --> 00:02:55.340
<i>LINE.07  Footsteps of Hope</i>

00:02:52.260 --> 00:02:54.800
I'm so hungry.

00:02:54.800 --> 00:02:57.490
You're really incredible, Naruko-kun.

00:02:58.470 --> 00:03:00.730
Ask me anything you want to know!

00:03:00.730 --> 00:03:01.940
I'm a genius—

00:03:01.940 --> 00:03:04.450
I'm here, Sakamichi!

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:06.300
It's Onoda-kun's typhoon mother!

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:07.490
You came again?!

00:03:07.850 --> 00:03:11.140
Yes, with the same housewife alliance.

00:03:11.140 --> 00:03:17.370
I wanted to see your race, but the 
roads were closed, so I just got here.

00:03:17.370 --> 00:03:19.500
Were they working on the roads or something?

00:03:19.500 --> 00:03:20.340
<i>That was the race!</i>

00:03:20.810 --> 00:03:22.990
So I went to the Toshogu Shrine instead!

00:03:22.990 --> 00:03:24.650
The Nikkou Tosho Shrine!

00:03:24.650 --> 00:03:27.500
And I had some yuba tofu skin 
with soy sauce and wasabi.

00:03:27.500 --> 00:03:30.020
It's so good! No wonder 
Nikkou is famous for it!

00:03:30.020 --> 00:03:32.450
What did you even come here to do?

00:03:32.450 --> 00:03:33.230
By the way...

00:03:33.610 --> 00:03:38.110
I see you're staying in the annex
instead of the fancy main hotel.

00:03:38.740 --> 00:03:41.170
Is that because your school
isn't private, but prefectural?

00:03:41.170 --> 00:03:43.530
D-Don't ask me!

00:03:44.210 --> 00:03:45.620
Is something going on?

00:03:45.620 --> 00:03:48.700
We're being raided by Onoda-kun's mother.

00:03:49.820 --> 00:03:50.910
Nice to meet you.

00:03:50.910 --> 00:03:53.200
I'm Koga, a third-year 
with the cycling club.

00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:55.230
Likewise, I'm Aoyagi.

00:03:55.230 --> 00:03:58.710
The third-years don't 
look as old this year.

00:03:58.710 --> 00:03:59.790
<i>This year?</i>

00:03:59.790 --> 00:04:01.010
<i>Does she mean...</i>

00:04:01.260 --> 00:04:03.010
<i>Kinjou-san?</i>

00:04:03.260 --> 00:04:06.300
Seriously, Mom! What are you even here for?

00:04:06.620 --> 00:04:11.020
Oh, right! I came to give this to you.

00:04:12.220 --> 00:04:14.170
Here, a tire pump!

00:04:14.170 --> 00:04:15.940
You forgot it!

00:04:15.940 --> 00:04:17.980
<i>No, I left it on purpose!</i>

00:04:17.980 --> 00:04:20.530
<i>And that's for a mommy bike, too!</i>

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:22.280
And...

00:04:22.710 --> 00:04:23.820
This, too.

00:04:24.620 --> 00:04:28.110
The sun can get in your eyes 
when you ride, right?

00:04:28.110 --> 00:04:30.600
So I bought you this!

00:04:30.600 --> 00:04:31.770
Best...

00:04:31.770 --> 00:04:32.750
...Boy?

00:04:32.750 --> 00:04:33.540
Not to worry!

00:04:33.540 --> 00:04:35.870
I have enough for everyone!

00:04:37.390 --> 00:04:41.730
If you wear those, you'll recognize
your teammates even from afar.

00:04:41.730 --> 00:04:44.150
It's a great idea, don't you think?

00:04:44.570 --> 00:04:46.390
Y-Yes.

00:04:47.230 --> 00:04:49.300
I'm sorry.

00:04:49.300 --> 00:04:50.780
I only have five left.

00:04:51.660 --> 00:04:53.300
When we got here...

00:04:53.300 --> 00:04:56.480
Oh, dear! Where is the annex?

00:04:56.480 --> 00:04:58.810
This one is so nice...

00:04:59.420 --> 00:05:03.070
Excuse me! Could you give 
us some directions?

00:05:03.850 --> 00:05:07.800
Oh, the annex is down this road.

00:05:07.800 --> 00:05:10.080
It's dark, so drive carefully.

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:13.120
You're such a nice boy!

00:05:13.120 --> 00:05:14.600
Please accept this.

00:05:14.600 --> 00:05:16.040
I'm sure it will come in handy.

00:05:16.990 --> 00:05:19.440
I gave him one.

00:05:21.250 --> 00:05:22.860
<b>Hakone Academy</b>

00:05:22.670 --> 00:05:26.660
Yes, I think his shirt said 
Hakone Academy on it.

00:05:26.660 --> 00:05:28.080
<i>H-Hakone Academy?!</i>

00:05:28.080 --> 00:05:31.180
<i>You were making trouble over there, too?!</i>

00:05:32.310 --> 00:05:34.730
It made me so happy...

00:05:36.180 --> 00:05:39.520
...when you said you'd 
work hard this year, too.

00:05:40.380 --> 00:05:44.150
I-I'm going to race again at the Inter-High.

00:05:45.300 --> 00:05:47.570
I'm going to Nikkou for three days.

00:05:49.620 --> 00:05:52.330
You worked so hard last year,

00:05:52.890 --> 00:05:56.410
but if you work too hard,
 you might burn yourself out.

00:05:56.810 --> 00:06:02.450
I was worried you'd say you wanted to quit.

00:06:05.670 --> 00:06:07.880
Live up to their expectations.

00:06:11.660 --> 00:06:12.850
Right.

00:06:15.190 --> 00:06:17.580
I went to the Toshogu Shrine.

00:06:17.580 --> 00:06:19.950
You just said that!

00:06:19.950 --> 00:06:22.520
I prayed...

00:06:23.250 --> 00:06:28.740
...that you would reach the goal
for these three days.

00:06:31.210 --> 00:06:31.820
<i>Goal...</i>

00:06:34.460 --> 00:06:36.040
Yes, thanks!

00:06:37.770 --> 00:06:41.040
You seem a little more reliable
than you were last year.

00:06:42.430 --> 00:06:45.290
You third-years,
 please take care of Sakamichi!

00:06:45.290 --> 00:06:45.840
Sure.

00:06:45.840 --> 00:06:47.990
Work hard in your anime club!

00:06:47.990 --> 00:06:49.050
We're the cycling club.

00:06:49.420 --> 00:06:52.320
Do you sing anime songs out loud, too?

00:06:52.320 --> 00:06:53.760
No, I don't.

00:06:55.430 --> 00:06:57.840
Okay, do your best!

00:06:57.840 --> 00:07:00.290
Kakegawa-san, let's head to the inn!

00:07:00.290 --> 00:07:04.400
They have three baths! How wonderful!

00:07:06.810 --> 00:07:08.360
The goal, eh?

00:07:08.360 --> 00:07:10.530
It's a long way off.

00:07:10.530 --> 00:07:12.490
We can't let our guard down, right, Onoda-kun?

00:07:17.770 --> 00:07:18.790
Yeah!

00:07:19.330 --> 00:07:21.170
Let's put our hearts into it!

00:07:26.250 --> 00:07:28.250
This is really cool.

00:07:28.250 --> 00:07:29.970
She has exquisite taste.

00:07:31.230 --> 00:07:34.070
It'll come in handy, eh?

00:07:34.740 --> 00:07:38.470
She was at the finish line last year.

00:07:39.450 --> 00:07:41.310
I'm looking forward to tomorrow.

00:07:41.810 --> 00:07:48.210
Let's ride full force when the 
time comes, Sakamichi-kun.

00:07:53.610 --> 00:07:55.490
<b>Nikkou Kihara Inn</b>

00:07:53.610 --> 00:07:55.490
<b>Kochikaiyo High School Cycling Club</b>

00:07:53.610 --> 00:07:55.490
<b>Kyoto Fushimi High School Cycling Club</b>

00:07:53.610 --> 00:07:55.490
<b>Yamagata Mogami High School Cycling Club</b>

00:07:53.610 --> 00:07:55.490
<b>Yamagata Mogami Alumni Meet</b>

00:07:53.610 --> 00:07:55.490
What? He's gone?

00:07:55.490 --> 00:07:59.240
We searched the whole inn, 
but couldn't find him.

00:07:59.240 --> 00:08:01.870
His bicycle is gone, too.

00:08:02.290 --> 00:08:06.260
Wh-Why?! Why did Midousuji-kun 
disappear again?!

00:08:06.260 --> 00:08:09.490
And Komari... I mean, Kishigami-kun 
is gone, as well.

00:08:09.490 --> 00:08:11.170
I don't care about him!

00:08:11.490 --> 00:08:14.420
Right now, everyone is to 
look for Midousuji-kun!

00:08:14.420 --> 00:08:15.370
Right!

00:08:16.910 --> 00:08:18.390
<i>Midousuji...</i>

00:08:19.780 --> 00:08:22.610
<i>You planned to win with 
a surprise breakaway.</i>

00:08:22.610 --> 00:08:25.930
<i>I heard you fought hard
up to the finish line.</i>

00:08:25.930 --> 00:08:28.110
<i>But you came in second.</i>

00:08:28.850 --> 00:08:31.000
<i>Only one can win the road race.</i>

00:08:31.000 --> 00:08:32.320
<i>Everyone else...</i>

00:08:32.980 --> 00:08:34.570
...is trash!

00:08:35.610 --> 00:08:36.850
<i>Midousuji...</i>

00:08:43.660 --> 00:08:46.910
<i>In spring, at dawn,</i>

00:08:47.460 --> 00:08:51.090
<i>it lightens little by little.</i>

00:08:51.090 --> 00:08:53.410
<i>Second place...</i>

00:08:53.410 --> 00:08:58.260
<i>Snow atop Fuji...</i>

00:08:58.260 --> 00:09:00.100
<i>Trash!</i>

00:09:00.100 --> 00:09:01.770
<i>Trash, trash!</i>

00:09:01.770 --> 00:09:03.390
<i>Trash, trash!</i>

00:09:03.390 --> 00:09:04.650
<i>Trash!</i>

00:09:04.650 --> 00:09:07.150
<i>Trash!</i>

00:09:35.590 --> 00:09:39.160
Tomorrow, at dawn,

00:09:39.160 --> 00:09:40.940
it will begin.

00:09:41.510 --> 00:09:44.300
How lovely.

00:09:44.300 --> 00:09:50.230
I'll overcome every one of those flies.

00:09:50.230 --> 00:09:53.110
No matter what!

00:09:55.610 --> 00:09:58.360
<i>Where... Where is Midousuji?</i>

00:09:58.760 --> 00:10:00.200
<i>He did something like this last year.</i>

00:10:00.550 --> 00:10:06.710
Sorry, but I'm quitting the 
Kyoto Fushimi Bicycle Club today.

00:10:07.250 --> 00:10:13.130
<i>I thought Ishigaki-san would handle it,
 that it wasn't my responsibility.</i>

00:10:16.020 --> 00:10:17.170
Midousuji!

00:10:21.230 --> 00:10:23.680
<i>But now that I'm a third-year, I understand.</i>

00:10:24.350 --> 00:10:29.310
<i>Without that monster Midousuji,
 our team would crumble in an instant.</i>

00:10:30.070 --> 00:10:33.350
<i>Ishigaki-san was doing his best
to keep us afloat.</i>

00:10:34.020 --> 00:10:35.050
<i>All alone.</i>

00:10:37.510 --> 00:10:40.490
<i>Ishigaki-san entrusted me...</i>

00:10:41.090 --> 00:10:45.040
Yama, you have to be 
Midousuji's conscience.

00:10:45.510 --> 00:10:49.790
<i>This is crazy, and I don't know if I can 
handle things like Ishigaki-san did.</i>

00:10:49.790 --> 00:10:50.620
<i>But...</i>

00:10:51.050 --> 00:10:53.100
<i>I'm going to find Midousuji.</i>

00:10:53.100 --> 00:10:53.960
<i>Then...</i>

00:10:54.570 --> 00:10:58.220
We're going to ride together tomorrow.
 Come back, Midousuji!

00:10:58.530 --> 00:11:00.260
<i>That's what I'll tell him.</i>

00:11:10.540 --> 00:11:12.190
That's your strategy?

00:11:12.610 --> 00:11:13.490
That's right.

00:11:13.490 --> 00:11:19.310
Kiriya, Funatsu, you two have to catch
everyone who breaks away from the pack!

00:11:19.310 --> 00:11:20.940
Uh, that's easier said than done.

00:11:20.940 --> 00:11:23.250
Catching all of them would be impossible.

00:11:23.250 --> 00:11:24.650
You'll do it!

00:11:24.650 --> 00:11:26.370
<i>This is my big chance!</i>

00:11:26.370 --> 00:11:30.750
<i>Without Midousuji here, I can become the ace!</i>

00:11:33.380 --> 00:11:35.790
Mizuta-kun!

00:11:35.790 --> 00:11:37.570
Midousuji-san!

00:11:37.570 --> 00:11:40.590
What do you think you're doing?

00:11:40.590 --> 00:11:45.730
You know not to have a meeting 
without my permission, correct?

00:11:45.730 --> 00:11:48.010
You aren't the leader.

00:11:48.010 --> 00:11:51.390
Y-Yes, Midousuji-kun!

00:11:53.630 --> 00:11:54.430
Kishigami!

00:11:54.430 --> 00:11:56.980
Where has he been?

00:11:57.950 --> 00:12:01.710
<i>He was on the reserves list at first,
but was later given a spot in the Inter-High.</i>

00:12:01.710 --> 00:12:05.290
<i>And at the end of day one, he caught up
to the leading pack like it was nothing.</i>

00:12:05.290 --> 00:12:09.940
<i>He's the biggest unknown here...
 Kishigami Komari.</i>

00:12:10.730 --> 00:12:11.620
What is it?

00:12:11.620 --> 00:12:13.150
N-Nothing.

00:12:11.620 --> 00:12:15.690
Huh? I can't understand you.

00:12:13.150 --> 00:12:15.690
We were wondering where you've been.

00:12:15.690 --> 00:12:16.990
Ah.

00:12:21.610 --> 00:12:23.680
<i>You're not going to answer?!</i>

00:12:26.830 --> 00:12:28.600
Huh? I see.

00:12:28.600 --> 00:12:30.420
Okay, I'll head back.

00:12:32.450 --> 00:12:36.440
Maybe he was just riding 
to blow off some steam.

00:12:36.440 --> 00:12:37.830
A false alarm, I guess.

00:12:39.940 --> 00:12:43.240
Sprint Point

00:12:39.940 --> 00:12:43.240
Phase 28

00:12:39.940 --> 00:12:43.240
Josanmo Panorama Road

00:12:39.940 --> 00:12:43.240
There are two crucial points.

00:12:43.590 --> 00:12:49.830
Anyone who falls out of line or
doesn't do as I say will get left behind.

00:12:49.830 --> 00:12:52.080
Ride like your lives depend on it.

00:12:52.080 --> 00:12:56.290
Tomorrow, we're definitely taking...

00:12:57.060 --> 00:12:58.340
the finish line!

00:12:58.670 --> 00:12:59.650
Yes, sir!

00:12:59.650 --> 00:13:02.510
Try to keep up, Komari.

00:13:00.010 --> 00:13:01.970
<i>Midousuji came back.</i>

00:13:02.510 --> 00:13:05.130
<i>He's riding on the second day.</i>

00:13:05.130 --> 00:13:07.550
<i>Our team is definitely getting closer...</i>

00:13:08.190 --> 00:13:09.230
<i>...to victory!</i>

00:13:11.190 --> 00:13:14.220
Are you sure, Yuki?

00:13:14.220 --> 00:13:15.060
Yeah.

00:13:15.400 --> 00:13:17.750
The Black Cat Deliveryman never dies.

00:13:19.570 --> 00:13:21.210
I'm riding tomorrow.

00:13:32.290 --> 00:13:33.660
Oh, you're right.

00:13:33.980 --> 00:13:38.130
It said "Goal" yesterday, 
but now it says "Start."

00:13:38.130 --> 00:13:38.790
Yep.

00:13:39.150 --> 00:13:42.840
They're going to have another 
day of that long battle.

00:13:43.820 --> 00:13:50.180
The third-years, the first-year, Naruko,
Imaizumi-kun, and four-eyes.

00:13:50.510 --> 00:13:51.640
Yes.

00:13:52.030 --> 00:13:55.530
It's a battle they only have one shot at.

00:13:56.310 --> 00:13:58.410
I hope they can pull it off.

00:13:58.410 --> 00:13:59.210
Yes.

00:14:01.060 --> 00:14:05.380
The second day of the Inter-High 
is about to start.

00:14:01.060 --> 00:14:05.590
<b>Inter-High Road Race</b>

00:14:08.950 --> 00:14:13.030
<b>Hakone
Academy</b>

00:14:10.490 --> 00:14:12.110
Hey, the riders are coming out!

00:14:12.110 --> 00:14:13.740
It's Hakone Academy!

00:14:14.420 --> 00:14:17.420
What's with that lame hat, Manami?

00:14:17.980 --> 00:14:20.000
Like it? It was a present.

00:14:20.420 --> 00:14:23.610
People sure like giving
 you things, Manami-san.

00:14:23.610 --> 00:14:24.570
You can't have it.

00:14:24.570 --> 00:14:25.890
I don't want it!

00:14:25.890 --> 00:14:29.710
Are you sure you won't give it away, Manami?

00:14:29.710 --> 00:14:30.760
Yes, of course not.

00:14:31.380 --> 00:14:32.890
Sounds like someone wants it!

00:14:33.270 --> 00:14:35.100
That's enough goofing around.

00:14:35.100 --> 00:14:36.810
<b>Hakone Academy</b>

00:14:36.020 --> 00:14:36.810
It's Kuroda!

00:14:36.810 --> 00:14:40.430
He fell yesterday while 
pushing their ace's back.

00:14:40.430 --> 00:14:41.860
Is he gonna ride?

00:14:41.860 --> 00:14:43.940
Look, there's Izumida, too!

00:14:44.300 --> 00:14:46.110
All six of them are here!

00:14:46.110 --> 00:14:47.590
What an impressive aura!

00:14:47.590 --> 00:14:50.750
They'll be this year's champions,
 Hakone Academy!

00:14:51.310 --> 00:14:52.640
<i>We're all ready.</i>

00:14:52.640 --> 00:14:54.930
<i>The team! Every member!</i>

00:14:54.930 --> 00:14:56.580
<i>I know even before they start riding.</i>

00:14:57.150 --> 00:15:00.330
<i>Doubashi's sprint, Manami's mountain climb,</i>

00:15:01.330 --> 00:15:03.650
<i>and Yuki's sacrificial run 
helped us achieve victory.</i>

00:15:04.290 --> 00:15:08.470
<i>That put the last piece 
of this team in place.</i>

00:15:09.490 --> 00:15:13.090
<i>This year's Hakone Academy team 
is revolving around Yuki.</i>

00:15:13.660 --> 00:15:14.810
<i>That suits me fine.</i>

00:15:15.340 --> 00:15:16.380
Abs, Yuki!

00:15:17.020 --> 00:15:19.290
We won all of the tags!

00:15:19.290 --> 00:15:21.440
But that's yesterday's news!

00:15:25.620 --> 00:15:27.440
We'll win them today, too!

00:15:28.330 --> 00:15:31.090
Don't get a big head!
Let's go Hakone Academy!

00:15:31.090 --> 00:15:32.490
Right!

00:15:35.220 --> 00:15:39.250
Getting first place in a road race 
changes your world overnight.

00:15:39.690 --> 00:15:41.230
What's that supposed to mean?

00:15:41.230 --> 00:15:43.530
There's a saying like that!

00:15:44.050 --> 00:15:48.910
Whether by coincidence or luck, 
victory means that much.

00:15:48.910 --> 00:15:51.780
And of course, it's a 
victory at the Inter-High.

00:15:52.290 --> 00:15:56.370
They have all of the colored tags.

00:15:56.370 --> 00:15:59.600
It gives them a powerful presence.

00:16:03.580 --> 00:16:07.820
What is it? Hakone Academy seem 
different from yesterday.

00:16:07.820 --> 00:16:10.690
Yeah, they're pumped up.

00:16:10.690 --> 00:16:13.280
That's the strength of those
who made good on their word.

00:16:13.730 --> 00:16:18.410
We have to watch out, or they'll 
start to control the race.

00:16:22.890 --> 00:16:25.570
But even so, we won't lose.

00:16:25.570 --> 00:16:29.500
This is good. The chase
 is always more exciting.

00:16:32.310 --> 00:16:35.470
Yeah, let's ride with everything we've got!

00:16:35.150 --> 00:16:38.180
<b>Mogu-mogu</b>

00:16:35.150 --> 00:16:38.180
<b>Rinko</b>

00:16:36.130 --> 00:16:38.180
I didn't zip my bag shut!

00:16:39.140 --> 00:16:41.060
You brought this stuff to a race?

00:16:41.060 --> 00:16:43.560
You sure you need that, Onoda-kun?

00:16:43.560 --> 00:16:46.690
It helps me calm down before I go to sleep.

00:16:45.440 --> 00:16:46.690
I guess you do!

00:16:46.690 --> 00:16:49.650
<b>Mogu-mogurinko</b>

00:16:47.390 --> 00:16:49.650
<i>That's Onoda Sakamichi.</i>

00:16:51.260 --> 00:16:54.000
<i>Last year was his first Inter-High.</i>

00:16:54.000 --> 00:16:57.180
<i>His first race, and he conquered 
the final mountain.</i>

00:16:57.180 --> 00:16:58.780
<i>They started calling him...</i>

00:16:59.540 --> 00:17:00.660
<i>The Mountain King.</i>

00:17:01.810 --> 00:17:04.180
<i>He doesn't look much like a king,</i>

00:17:04.180 --> 00:17:07.920
<i>and he seems completely defenseless
when he's not on his bike.</i>

00:17:08.280 --> 00:17:10.650
Oh, there it is.

00:17:10.650 --> 00:17:12.380
Thank goodness.

00:17:12.830 --> 00:17:18.120
They say everyone who goes to see you after
hearing the rumors doesn't recognize you,

00:17:18.120 --> 00:17:19.720
and I guess that must be true.

00:17:22.270 --> 00:17:24.810
<i>Wow, it's a cool guy!</i>

00:17:27.580 --> 00:17:28.190
Click.

00:17:29.590 --> 00:17:30.650
Kawhap!

00:17:33.050 --> 00:17:36.740
That was how my brother 
said he'd beat someone.

00:17:38.050 --> 00:17:41.340
Huh? Maybe it was "kapow" instead of "kawhap."

00:17:41.820 --> 00:17:45.510
You know my brother, Shinkai Hayato, right?

00:17:45.510 --> 00:17:46.580
Hayato-kun?

00:17:47.730 --> 00:17:49.500
Shinkai-san?

00:17:49.810 --> 00:17:52.300
My name's Yuto.

00:17:53.220 --> 00:17:54.370
I'm a first-year.

00:17:54.820 --> 00:17:55.380
Thank you.

00:17:56.040 --> 00:17:58.550
My team doesn't know this, but...

00:18:00.620 --> 00:18:03.970
I came to the Inter-High to challenge you.

00:18:05.910 --> 00:18:09.440
I was ordered to stop you if you made
a move in the mountains yesterday.

00:18:09.950 --> 00:18:12.190
Unfortunately, I didn't get the chance.

00:18:13.610 --> 00:18:17.110
Let's race at some point today.

00:18:18.500 --> 00:18:19.820
R-Race?

00:18:19.820 --> 00:18:23.830
Is your answer yes, Mountain King?

00:18:26.020 --> 00:18:27.830
"Mountain King"?

00:18:28.150 --> 00:18:30.540
It's your nickname.

00:18:30.940 --> 00:18:32.500
<i>Nickname?</i>

00:18:32.990 --> 00:18:36.090
My nickname is the Peak Spider!

00:18:39.270 --> 00:18:42.420
A nickname? For me?

00:18:42.420 --> 00:18:44.720
That's great news! Mountain King, you said?

00:18:45.650 --> 00:18:48.890
Is that like "see-king" mountains to climb?

00:18:49.310 --> 00:18:51.140
That's not bad at all!

00:18:51.140 --> 00:18:56.640
But, an animal... A name with a 
bug in it would have been nice.

00:18:56.640 --> 00:19:02.030
No, the supreme king of the mountain,
the ruler of its peak.

00:19:02.940 --> 00:19:04.990
The king?

00:19:05.990 --> 00:19:07.870
<i>Mountain King?</i>

00:19:07.870 --> 00:19:10.310
You're strong.

00:19:10.310 --> 00:19:15.010
Even yesterday, you broke through 
several teams, climbed the mountain,

00:19:15.010 --> 00:19:17.010
and caught up to the leading pack at the end.

00:19:18.010 --> 00:19:21.130
N-No, Imaizumi-kun just said I could go.

00:19:21.130 --> 00:19:23.180
And Teshima-san helped me, too.

00:19:23.180 --> 00:19:25.620
I didn't do anything that great.

00:19:25.620 --> 00:19:28.250
It was really a team effort...

00:19:26.420 --> 00:19:28.250
<i>So this is the Mountain King.</i>

00:19:28.250 --> 00:19:30.320
<i>A truly self-unaware climber.</i>

00:19:30.320 --> 00:19:31.180
But...

00:19:31.770 --> 00:19:35.300
I would really prefer an animal nickname.

00:19:35.300 --> 00:19:36.520
<i>That's what you want?</i>

00:19:36.520 --> 00:19:40.900
Hey, #16 from Hakone Academy and 
the Mountain King are talking!

00:19:40.900 --> 00:19:43.670
Do they know each other? 
Let's get a picture!

00:19:44.980 --> 00:19:45.950
<i>So close!</i>

00:19:46.690 --> 00:19:49.450
I don't want people talking 
about this, so I'll be going.

00:19:49.450 --> 00:19:51.230
Let's talk on the road.

00:19:54.910 --> 00:19:56.810
Um, Shinkai-kun....

00:19:57.260 --> 00:20:00.900
Oh, yeah. You didn't give me
an answer to my challenge.

00:20:00.900 --> 00:20:02.340
It's "yes," right?

00:20:02.340 --> 00:20:03.680
Oh, not that.

00:20:03.980 --> 00:20:06.600
Do you have a nickname, too?

00:20:09.090 --> 00:20:13.100
Yes, I do. It's not that famous yet, though.

00:20:19.700 --> 00:20:21.370
The Peak Hornet.

00:20:24.540 --> 00:20:27.230
Peak... Hornet?

00:20:29.020 --> 00:20:30.910
It'll hurt if I sting you.

00:20:35.690 --> 00:20:37.450
Onoda-kun, time to go!

00:20:37.450 --> 00:20:39.130
We'll lose our warm-up time.

00:20:39.550 --> 00:20:40.870
Oh, right.

00:20:43.790 --> 00:20:49.010
<i>Shinkai Yuto-kun... He seems strong.</i>

00:20:49.860 --> 00:20:53.690
<i>Sorry, Shinkai-kun, but I can't race you.</i>

00:20:54.490 --> 00:20:57.190
<i>Teshima-san told me this morning.</i>

00:20:57.600 --> 00:21:01.190
We don't have a single second 
to spare in today's race!

00:21:01.810 --> 00:21:04.200
All six of us will ride...

00:21:04.540 --> 00:21:07.660
for the second day of the Inter-High!

00:21:07.660 --> 00:21:10.650
<i>Five minutes until the race starts!</i>

00:21:10.650 --> 00:21:13.470
<i>All of the racers are lined up
at the starting line.</i>

00:21:13.470 --> 00:21:14.710
Good luck!

00:21:14.710 --> 00:21:17.540
<i>The strongest contenders must be this team!</i>

00:21:17.540 --> 00:21:20.290
<i>They won all of the colored tags yesterday</i>

00:21:20.290 --> 00:21:22.800
<i>and restored their title
 as champions, Hakone Academy!</i>

00:21:22.800 --> 00:21:25.690
<i>Next are two teams which came 
close but could not prevail,</i>

00:21:25.690 --> 00:21:29.360
<i>Sohoku High School and Kyoto Fushimi.</i>

00:21:29.360 --> 00:21:32.300
<i>All of the teams are focusing on today!</i>

00:21:36.140 --> 00:21:41.450
<i>The Inter-High's second day race
 is about to begin!</i>

00:23:13.950 --> 00:23:14.970
Ow...

00:23:17.220 --> 00:23:17.930
Here!

00:23:18.450 --> 00:23:19.780
That hurts! Knock it off!

00:23:20.580 --> 00:23:21.630
Don't laugh!

00:23:23.580 --> 00:23:26.670
Yuki-chan, you need to
soak up to your shoulders.

00:23:26.670 --> 00:23:30.370
Yuki, you must relieve your fatigue 
so you can race tomorrow.

00:23:30.370 --> 00:23:32.390
Hey... stop!

00:23:30.990 --> 00:23:33.760
It'll feel good!

00:23:36.530 --> 00:23:39.980
<i>NEXT LINE  Second Day, Start!</i>

00:23:39.980 --> 00:23:44.980
This is a work of fiction. All characters and organizations
 appearing in this work are fictional. In this work,
 characters sometimes engage in dangerous activities.
 While riding bicycles on actual roads,
 please follow all traffic laws and ride safely.

00:23:44.980 --> 00:23:51.250
<b>Mountain</b>

00:23:44.980 --> 00:23:51.250
<b>King</b>

00:23:44.980 --> 00:23:51.250
<b>Mura</b>
